ef 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186051070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428679 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428680 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1031 "Double Integrals Over Type II Regions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1033 2152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1034 0.9693814428704701 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "3ab583b8-5390-5f48-b28b-1a89db70664f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050822 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050822 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050822 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050822 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050822 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050822 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050822 #edb/ref 1031 "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050822 #edb/ref 1033 1979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050822 #edb/ref 1034 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050822 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "6961ffb7-2e37-5f54-ac39-0331f4517bbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051070 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051070 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051070 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051070 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050694 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051070 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133882 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051070 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051070 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051070 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428635 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051070 #edb/ref 1031 "Introduction to Green's Theorem" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051070 #edb/ref 1033 2116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051070 #edb/ref 1034 1.061673902190143 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051070 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7e860cf4-4488-5596-ab86-e913faeb242e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186131875 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186131875 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475713 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186131875 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186131875 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186131875 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186131875 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186131875 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186131875 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186475776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186131875 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2cda2ff4-5dd7-546b-a1e2-111a796413b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133653 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7134" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133653 #edb/ref 1071 "If $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=\\sqrt{x-2}$ and $y=1-x$ from $y=0$ to $y=1,$ as shown below, then what is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D (x^2y+xy^2) \\, \\mathrm{d}A$ expressed as a repeated integral?\n\n![](images/0e/0e4cf57408f9ca18dc4613317b8b9bc8b3149da0bf273ad03a8a8a48a6e6f454.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133653 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "792b0c63-15eb-5b0e-b5d6-01ae5b68eeca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133653 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y=\\sqrt{x-2}$ and $y=1-x$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=\\sqrt{x-2} & \\,⟹\\,x={y}^{2}+2 \\\\ y=1-x & \\,⟹\\,x=1-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/f0/f0e531c612c84aa0260b318aa1fbe21c9089270b8c4a1079e08583b7fc5a5d90.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\quad 1-y \\leq x  \\leq y^2+2 \\bigg\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{{y}^{2}+2}({x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133654 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7135" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133654 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed between the curves $y=x^2$ and $y=3-2x$ below the line $y=3.$ What is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} f\\left( {x,y} \\right) \\, \\mathrm{d}A\\:$ expressed as a repeated integral?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133654 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e005ebb9-6c14-529e-be8f-9b837e45eef1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133654 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](images/ff/ffbe0db1ae1bb082e63b0d97324b43dd78334dfbd1e88aaa0744be039dd0efc6.png)\n\nWe need to represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y=x^2$ and $y=3-2x$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y} \\\\ y=3-2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{3-y}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{y} & =\\frac{3-y}{2} \\\\ 4y & =(3-y)^{2} \\\\ 4y & =9-6y+{y}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2}-10y+9 & =0 \\\\ (y-1)(y-9) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies below the line $y=3,$ the $y$-limits are \n\n$$\n1 \\le y \\le 3.\n$$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/3c/3c56798a33ee2da6d928174b67546945be4bf3594d15e89f3ca39119dd4e2c62.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 3, \\quad \\dfrac{3-y}{2} \\leq x  \\leq \\sqrt{y} \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{(3-y)/2}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133655 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7136" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133655 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{\\sqrt{\\pi}}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi}} \\int_0^{y^2} \\frac{\\sin y^2}{y} \\, \\mathrm{d}x \\,\\mathrm{d}y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133655 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ebd5bc16-2df2-5014-a1a2-bdebf2afa195" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133655 #edb/ref 1074 "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}}{y}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}}{y}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}}{y}[x]_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}}{y}({y}^{2}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}y\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}\\,dy & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{2}]}_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133656 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7137" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133656 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} xy^2\\,\\mathrm{d}A,\\:$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves $x^2+y^2=4$ and $x=0,$ and above the line $y=-1,$ as shown in the picture.\n\n![](images/f9/f93aeee59ad97fde0efceff342e32a19062187261abec865616bfa963f1084a6.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133656 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ad2ef01a-d49d-5b17-9066-d5c3970caf31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133656 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x \\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}} \\\\ x=0 & \\,⟹\\,x=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 4-{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the line $y=-1,$ the $y$-limits are \n$-1 \\le y \\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/8d/8d77e3caa18191710e056b72ea54e5820e6244d9e90719222deed409d3992c5b.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\quad 0 \\leq x  \\leq \\sqrt{4-y^2} \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\iint \\limits_{D} xy^2\\,\\mathrm{d}A = \\int_{-1}^2 \\int_0^{\\sqrt{4-y^2}}\\, xy^2\\, \\mathrm dx\\,   \\mathrm{d}  y\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,x{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}x\\,dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{y}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}(4-{y}^{2}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}(2{y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(2{y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2})\\,dy & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-\\frac{{y}^{5}}{10}]}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{32}{10})-(-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186268862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351280 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186380985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186380992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186382441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186475949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186475963 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1039 "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral When the Limits are Given" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186133653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133838 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "40bbc65e-5ee4-5ce6-aaf7-d0f9968c0c51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133839 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218