86268539 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268539 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268539 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186266902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268539 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4d60afa9-e4b7-51f3-8fee-bda29b300a3d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268862 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268862 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132402" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268862 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268862 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/bf/bfa591e51f42e8e52b67e61c23b02ea69b03bdecc1c4b815370ce6b2b0b5f213.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the $x$-axis and the curves $x={y}^{2}-4$ and $x=4-{y}^{2},$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268862 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3cfac5a9-6edd-563f-8792-0eaf27928ce8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268862 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/85/85d3faac9a27353a8ea5151b3a32f1065aecb02fd07e0b20727c35de0a7fb216.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,{y}^{2}-4\\le x\\le 4-{y}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-4}^{4-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-4}^{4-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268873 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268873 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132531" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268873 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268873 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,dA,$ where $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268873 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2da71a28-356e-5389-9334-828f80b33c46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268873 #edb/ref 1074 "The integral is defined over a type II region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}\\}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{x}^{2}\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}(\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{6}-0)dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{5}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{5}\\,dy & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{5}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{6}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{32}{3}-\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{21}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321167 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321167 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321167 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "022db7d6-74f8-5b70-953b-f7307b30d216" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322638 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322638 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322638 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bfcc41a0-cba5-52a7-ad10-f699b98332a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322902 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322902 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218632290